"""ant-facet-test: replicate-level facet tests by pseudobulk limma-voom (v3, exploratory).

What it does
------------
For every eligible dataset (primary, in a facet scope that is tested: human post-mortem
tissue, mouse in vivo or human cells xenografted into mouse; not in vitro or bulk; a
raw-counts layer; at least 4 replicates) and every cell type stratum, tests the facets
that the dataset's scope allows (``lib/facet_scopes.py``, ``facet_scopes`` of the facet
registry) for differential gene expression. The unit of replication is the dataset's
replicate (donor, animal, sample):

  * sex           ant_sex            male vs female (reference female)
  * disease       ant_disease        AD vs control (reference control); every
                                     other value is dropped. PROVISIONAL:
                                     the disease vocabulary decisions
                                     (audit L17 to L21) are still open.
  * apoe4_carrier  ant_apoe4_carrier   e4 carrier vs non-carrier (reference
                                     non-carrier); derived from ant_apoe when
                                     the carrier column is absent
  * braak         ant_braak          numeric linear trend per Braak unit
  * age           ant_age            numeric linear trend per decade (age / 10);
                                     model ~ age + sex + pmi [+ batch]: the age effect
                                     includes the effect of disease prevalence
  * app_nlgf      ant_app_nlgf       App NL-G-F knock-in vs control (reference control),
                                     mouse in vivo and xenograft hosts; covariate sex
                                     (host sex for a xenograft)

Pipeline per dataset (see doc/DESIGN_facet_testing.md for the rationale)::

  .md api config --build_obs_view_sql--> TEMP obs views on a read-only
  attach of the .duckdb (the CURRENT mapping, not the stored views)
  -> donor table (one value per facet per donor; conflicting donors dropped)
  -> pseudobulk counts per (donor, cell type) from the counts by_gene
     parquet, summed in DuckDB; donors with several samples are collapsed
     by summing; (donor, cell type) groups with < 10 cells are dropped
  -> bin/annot/facet_test_limma.R: filterByExpr, TMM, voom, lmFit, eBayes,
     per (dataset, cell type, facet), BH within that triple
  -> <h5adstore>/_facet_tests/<group>/<file>.facet_tests.parquet,
     <file>.facet_composition.parquet and <file>.facet_run_manifest.json

Inputs: the h5adstore (read only: .md, .h5ad.mus, .duckdb, counts sidecar).
Outputs: only under <h5adstore>/_facet_tests/. Nothing else in data/ is
written; .h5ad / .duckdb / .md files are never opened for writing.

Usage::

  ant-facet-test inventory [--out tsv]
  ant-facet-test run --db-id K22/AST [--facets sex,disease,age,app_nlgf] [--out-root DIR]
  ant-facet-test run --all [--facets ...] [--max-load 12]
  ant-facet-test run --pool madrc_myeloid     # donor-pooled unit (cohort table, column pool_members)
  ant-facet-test summarize --out-dir DIR [--genes PTPRG,...]   # replication tables per facet scope

Needs an R with limma and edgeR (``--rscript`` or $ANT_FACET_RSCRIPT, default
envs/facet-test-r/bin/Rscript). The anthive-data env has neither package.
"""
